ty spirit and provide assistance to identified learners in need; NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, that the University of Antique Student Government shall conduct a Community Outreach Program at Barangay Lapaz and Barangay Pitac, Tibiao Antique; RESOLVED, the members of the student body have expressed their full support for the conduct of this activity, recognizing its significance in fostering compassion, generosity, and community engagement; RESOLVED FURTHER, the UASG request the utilization of UA-TLMC Truck or any available vehicles to be use in transporting the school supplies and snacks at the Brgy. Lapaz and Tino. RESOLVED FURTHER, that copies of this resolution be furnished to the Office of the Campus Director, Office of the Director for Administration and Finance, the Office of Student Affairs and Services, and other concerned offices for their approval and support. I hereby certified in the correctness of the foregoing resolution. Certified True and Correct: JENNIFER D. AVE Executive Secretary, UASG Attested: ERIKA GYNNE B. NABAS President, UASG Noted: NINIA ROSE M. ETORCITA, MSCS Adviser, UASG JEFFREY T. IMPORTANTE, MAEd                                              Co-Adviser, UASG                                                  Recommending approval: JOSE N. MAGBANUA, PhD Coordinator, Student Affairs and Services CHARLENE JOY R. AMAR, PhD Director of Academic Affairs  JULIET D. SALVACION, MPA Director for Administration and Finance Approved by: PORFERIO S. BANGCAYA, PhD Campus Director  EXCERPTS FROM THE MINUTES OF THE SPECIAL MEETING OF THE UNIVERSITY OF ANTIQUE STUDENT GOVERNMENT HELD ON NOVEMBER 23, 2025, FROM 2:00 TO 4:30 PM VIA ZOOM PRESENT: 28 ABSENT: 15 Resolution Author: BRAIN JECK G. REYNO               BLGA Representative, UASG LIST OF OFFICERS President: Erika Gynne B. Nabas Vice President: Marichu T. Lapesora Senators: Jupet F. Espartero Nicole Pongyan Jay Razel C. Fransisco Reuel Nathaniel M. Alvarez Roger J. Coria Florence Rameli G. Bandoja N