organizations to develop effective leadership skills, knowledge, and practices. It helps students develop strategic thinking, problem-solving, and decision-making skills, enabling them to navigate complex situations and drive organizational success. Anent to this, we would like to invite you, Honorable, to be one of our guest speakers to discussed ideas or strategies, and steps in making a concrete resolution letter.  Your presence would greatly inspire and delight the student leaders of UA-TLMC. We hope you can join us and be part of the success of this upcoming event. We sincerely look forward to see you and gain knowledge from you that can help us enhance our leadership skills.  Objectives: To elect competent, service-oriented, and visionary student leaders who will represent the collective voice of the student body. To foster participatory democracy and transparency within student governance. To provide a platform for emerging leaders to practice responsible leadership and good governance in preparation for future national and community service. Participants: UASG                 (46) Adviser                 (2) ROTC                  (32) COMELEC Assistants (33) TOTAL:               113 Budget Allocation ITEM QUANTITY PRICE AMOUNT A. SNACKS Tetra Pack Juice 12 120 1,440.00 Cheese Burger 113 32 3,616.00 TOTAL 5,056.00 SOURCE OF FUND UASG FUND                                                                                                     Php 30, 000 JERU AVRIL N. CRUZ UASG, Chief Justice UASG, COMELEC Chairman Noted: NINIA ROSE M. ETORCITA, MSCS UASG ADVISER JEFFREY T. IMPORTANTE, MAEd                                   UASG CO-ADVISER Funds Available: NORELEE MAE N. PAGSUGUIRON Administrative Officer IV Recommending Approval: JOSE N. MAGBANUA, PhD. SAS Coordinator CHARLENE JOY R. AMAR, PhD. OIC Director, Academic Affairs JULIET D. SALVACION, MPA Director, Administrative and Finance Approved: PORFERIO S. BANGCAYA, PhD. Campus Director',343,'Resolution',20.00,'[]','[]','null','{\"method\": \"Pattern Matching\", \"category\": \"Resolution\", \"entities\": [], \"keywords\": [], \"provider\": \"Keyword Fallback\", \"sentiment\": [], \"confidence\": 20}','nlpcloud',5363,'2026-05-22 12:54:24'),(260,264,'Office of Student Affairs and Services UNIVERSITY OF ANTIQUE STUDENT GOVERNMENT tlmc.uasg@antiquespride.edu.ph Resolution No. 13, series of 2025 A RESOLUTION TO CONDUCT A COMMUNITY OUTREACH PROGRAM AT BARANGAY, LAPAZ AND BARANGAY PITAC, TIBIAO, ANTIQUE. WHEREAS, the University of Antique Student Government serves as a medium of expression for student ideals; WHEREAS, the student body acknowledges its responsibility to strengthen its commitment to community engagement and extend social involvement; WHEREAS, the student body decided to conduct a Community Outreach Program to be held at Barangay Lapaz and Barangay Pitac, Tibiao Antique; WHEREAS, the said activity aims to foster community spirit and provide assistance to identified learners in need; NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED, that the University of Antique Student Government shall conduct a Community Outreach Program at Barangay Lapaz and Barangay Pitac, Tibiao Antique; RESOLVED, the members of the student body have expressed their full support for the conduct of this activity, recognizing its significance in fostering compassion, generosity, and community engagement; RESOLVED FURTHER, the UASG request the utilization of UA-TLMC Truck or any available vehicles to be use in transporting the school supplies and snacks at the Brgy. Lapaz and Tino. RESOLVED FURTHER, that copies of this resolution be furnished to the Office of the Campus Director, Office of the Director for Administration and Finance, the Office of Student Affairs and Services, and other concerned offices for their approval and support. I hereby certified in the correctness of the foregoing resolution. Certified True and Correct: JENNIFER D. AVE Executive Secretary, UASG Attested: ERIKA GYNNE B. NABAS President, UASG Noted: NINIA ROSE M. ETORCITA, MSCS Adviser, UASG JEFFREY T. IMPORTANTE, MAEd                                              Co-Adviser, UASG                                                  Recommending approval: JOSE N. MAGBANUA, PhD Coordinator, Student Affairs and Services CHARLENE JOY R. AMAR, PhD Director of Academic Affairs  JULIET D. SALVACION, MPA Director for Administration and Finance Approved by: PORFERIO S. BANGCAYA, PhD Campus Director  EXCERPTS FROM THE MINUTES OF THE SPECIAL MEETING OF THE UNIVERSITY OF ANTIQUE STUDENT GOVERNMENT HELD ON NOVEMBER 23, 2025, FROM 2:00 TO 4:30 PM VIA ZOOM PRESENT: 28 ABSENT: 15 Resolution Author: BRAIN JECK G. REYNO               BLGA Representative, UASG LIST OF OFFICERS President: Erika Gynne B. Nabas Vice President: Marichu T. Lapesora Senators: Jupet F. Espartero Nicole Pongyan Jay Razel C. Fransisco Reuel Nathaniel M. Alvarez Roger J. Coria Florence Rameli G. Bandoja Nemfa P. Ponayo Pablito B. Samillano Jr. Edcel John B. Marquez Riza P. Arnaiz Jerald T. Barrientos James Isaac F. Guantia Representatives:LHS (JHS): Celeste Marie I. FloresLHS (SHS): Andrea Leigh P. EroCTE (BEED): Arrianne E. NabasCTE (BSED): Roxanne Jane S. Motus  CBM (BSHM): James Francis F. Garcia CBM (BLGA): Brain Jeck G. Reyno CBM (BSE): Divony V. Majabague CCS (BSIS): Lorie E. BelarioCCS (BSCS): Greg A. Labrador CCS (BSIT): Kate E. CalawodCOF(BSFi): Kim Jenny Pearl D. Samar Executive Branch:Secretary: Jennifer D. AveTreasurer: Marrianne PagsuguironAuditor: Princess Mae D. NabasBusiness Manager: Jan Russell Amar Asst. Business Manager: Jhero M. AlorroInternal Affairs Officer: Raiza Mae DoloricaExternal Affairs Officer: Kirstie GindapPRO: Cedrick Jay C. Dela CruzAssistant PRO: Jiezel A. SamillanoJudicial Branch: Chief Justice: Jeru Avril N. CruzJudicial Secretary: Rejie E. BarcebalJudicial Deputy: Menard CristobasJudicial Members:1. Bryan Jhon M. Dubria2. Estelito T.  Amar3. Ma. Jeandy O. Española4. Rinalie Blas',527,'Resolution',95.00,'[]','[]','null','{\"method\": \"Pattern Matching\", \"category\": \"Resolution\", \"entities\": [], \"keywords\": [], \"provider\": \"Keyword Fallback\", \"sentiment\": [], \"confidence\": 95}','nlpcloud',3983,'2026-05-22 12:55:40'),(261,265,'OFFICE OF STUDENT AFFAIRS AND SERVICES           UNIVERSITY OF ANTIQUE STUDENT GOVERNMENT          tlmc.uasg@antiquespride.edu.ph March 13, 2025 ANGEL B. BIADORA NSTP Coordinator  University of Antique Tario-Lim Memorial Campus Greetings! The University of Antique Student Government (UASG) serves as a medium of expression for the ideals and aspirations of every student of the University, promotes, and protects student’s welfare and interest, develops their potentials, skills, and dynamic leadership by organizing and carrying out school activities, service projects, and plan events that contribute for the welfare of the school and the community. In line with this, the UASG will conduct a Leadership Training 2025 with a theme, “Empowering YoUng LeAders: Celebrating Tradition and Culture” on April 4-5, 2025 at the Recreational and Fitness Center (RFC). Moreover, this training aims to develop leadership skills, teamwork, and discipline among the participants. Furthermore, I am writing this letter to formally request the assistance of 25 ROTC officers. We believe that the presence and guidance of the ROTC officers will significantly enhance the program by providing assistance to maintain order all throughout the said event. The ROTC officers will also take part in the event which will foster participation and collaboration between the UASG and the ROTC. We are hoping for your kind and favorable consideration on this matter. Thank you very much! Very truly yours, ESTELITO T. AMAR UASG, Senator Noted by: NINIA ROSE M. ETORCITA Adviser, UASG JEFFREY T. IMPORTANTE, MAEd Co-Adviser, UASG Recommending Approval: ANGEL B. BIADORA Coordinator, NSTP Approved: PORFERIO S. BANGCAYA, PhD Campus Director',251,'Proposal',30.00,'[]','[]','null','{\"method\": 